            <div xml:id="d541">

                <pb facs="0787" n="671" xml:id="pg671"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1123 Lincheng/186: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-06-29T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29,
                                1923—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 29—7:47
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>241. Your 126, June 26, 6 p.m. Conformably to your 116 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >118</hi>], June 21, 6 p.m., at a meeting of the committee morning of 25th I
                    notified committee that you disapproved proposed demands with respect to
                    Shanghai and I accordingly requested as everything in the report was provisional
                    and tentative that Shanghai section be stricken out. Committee in general
                    recognized your reasoning as unanswerable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
